  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Safety Management Policy Competence of Agro-Livestick and Fishery Products for Asian Developing Countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Its primary goal is to strengthen food safety management policies in Asian countries, enhance public health, and facilitate policy and information exchange. The project also aims to build a regional expert network and boost Korean food exports. To achieve these objectives, government officials from Asian countries are invited to Korea for training on food safety management policies through lectures and site visits to domestic food manufacturing and management facilities. This initiative promotes the excellence of Korean food products, supports export expansion, and provides benchmarking opportunities for safety management systems. As part of a mid-term plan (20262030), the project will annually select target countries and participants to implement both invitational training in Korea and on-site training in recipient countries, offering tailored education to meet their specific needs.</narrative>
  </description>
